NAND Flash is a non-volatile memory technology that retains stored information even when power is disconnected. Its combination of high storage density, fast data access, and compact design makes it essential to modern digital infrastructure. It is widely used in smartphones, personal computers, memory cards, USB drives, industrial equipment, and enterprise storage systems.

The market is benefiting from the growing volume of digital information generated by connected devices, online services, enterprise applications, and artificial intelligence workloads. As organisations seek faster access to data and more efficient storage infrastructure, SSD adoption continues to create opportunities for NAND Flash suppliers.

